  "overall_assessment": "The direct G\u2084 = G_N test FAILS as expected \u2014 this is the hierarchy problem, not a framework failure. The framework parameterizes gravity as G\u2084 = \u03b1/(2K\u00b2) but cannot close the 10^38 gap between QCD and gravitational couplings. POSITIVE findings: (1) K_naive = 18 predicts quark spin fraction = 33%, matching measured ~30%. (2) Lattice QCD g_eff crossover at T_c confirms the framework's K tracks deconfinement. (3) Nuclear shell model DOF modestly improves alpha-decay predictions when used as K divisor. The interesting structure is in the K RATIOS and the spin crisis prediction, not in the absolute G\u2084 value."
